-- title:
--   Coset graph at a split prime versus Bruhat–Tits tree, equivariantly
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $q'$ be a prime such that $\mathbb{H}=\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every $v$ in the height-one spectrum of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, every nonzero element of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a unit precisely when $q'\in v$. Let $N\neq 0$ and let $R\subseteq\mathbb{H}$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_i$ with the relative index of $R$ in $\Lambda_1$ equal to $N$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q'$ and $r\nmid N$, and let $v$ be a place with $r\in v$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R r`: $n$ lies in the finite adelic box of $R$, so does $r\cdot n^{-1}$, while $n^{-1}$ and $r^{-1}n$ do not. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $r$ a nonunit of $A$, write $K_0=$ `ratClosure A` for the topological closure of the prime subfield inside the completion of $A$'s valuation, and let $R_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with a $K_0$-algebra structure making $K_0$ its fraction field, whose image in $K_0$ consists exactly of the elements of valuation $\le 1$ in that completion. Let $\iota:\mathbb{H}\to M_2(K_0)$ be an injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map and $\rho:\mathbb{H}^\times\to \mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$ the monoid homomorphism sending $x$ to the class of $\iota(x)$. Then there exist an isomorphism $e$ of simple graphs from the coset graph `CosetGraph.graph R v` at $v$ with shift the $v$-component of $n$ — vertices the quotient of $(\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v)^\times$ by the level group generated by the local box units of $R$ at $v$ together with the scalar units, and $[g]$ adjacent to $[gkn_v]$ for $k$ in the level group — onto the Bruhat–Tits tree of $R_0$-lattices in $K_0^2$, and a group isomorphism $\psi$ from `ProjAwayUnits R v`, the quotient of the group of units of $\mathbb{H}$ that are local units of $R$ at all places $w\neq v$ by the kernel of its action, onto the image $\rho(\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R\,v)$ in $\mathrm{PGL}(2,K_0)$, such that: $e$ is $\mathbb{H}^\times$-equivariant in the sense $e([\,\iota_v(g)\,y\,])=\rho(g)\cdot e([y])$ for all $g\in\mathbb{H}^\times$ and all units $y$ of $\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$; $\psi$ sends the class of $\gamma$ to $\rho(\gamma)$; $e(\gamma\cdot x)=\psi(\gamma)\cdot e(x)$ for all $\gamma$ in `ProjAwayUnits R v` and all vertices $x$; and for every dart $d$ of the coset graph the stabiliser of the image dart in $\rho(\mathrm{awayUnits}\,R\,v)$ and the stabiliser of $d$ in `ProjAwayUnits R v` have the same cardinality.
--
--   This is the dictionary between the adelic coset-graph description of the Hecke data of an Eichler order at a prime $r$ of good reduction and the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{PGL}_2$ over the closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ in a completion of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at a place above $r$, together with the identification of the acting group and the matching of dart stabilisers, as needed for the Čerednik–Drinfel'd/Mumford–Kurihara uniformisation. It is used by the subsequent results comparing quotients of the graph with the class set of $R$ and producing level subgroups with finite, torsion-controlled stabilisers.
